      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that pathways to citizenship drive economic stability is a well-intentioned but ultimately flawed premise. While integration is a goal, it cannot be achieved if the system is porous and lacks legal structure. A stable workforce is built on legal, orderly immigration, not on an influx that overwhelms infrastructure and strains social services. True economic stability comes from a predictable, controlled environment where labor supply matches demand under the rule of law.",
